 "rules": "T14 step 9: verdict of one front-back level (two robots solved by role_solve.py --construction frontback). Read only, CPU.\n\nSame verdict as step 8 (shared_eval.evaluate: V0 gravity on S, non-hand penetration, two-robot clearance, section-4 contact\nretention >= 0.99; Section 4's penetration criterion has no baseline and is not used), with two items as Kevin set them:\n  * support drift (Kevin 2026-11-24 18:40 item 1, the step-8 re-judge): V0 quantity and limit (step8_rejudge.added_drift, 0.01 m),\n    windows = each role's own person's support segments of round 6 (support.py on the solve's saved human joints). Source robot\n    of role 0 = the source solve at the same frame; of role 1 = the source solve played backwards in time (the partner's legs\n    are the demonstration's legs reversed and turned about the vertical: a rigid motion, the same feet). The step-8 window\n    values are kept as information (old_window_*). --r1-source construction (step 9e): role 1's source at frame t = the\n    source solve at the construction's source frame, moved by the same rigid map (gates r1_source), so that it matches\n    constructions that reverse only the walking segment (the whole-clip-reversed value is kept as information).\n  * main motion (Kevin 2026-11-25: the screen's class-a threshold): pelvis net horizontal displacement over the clip / s > 1.0 m,\n    for the two persons (pre-solve gate, step9_gates.py) and for the two solved robots (root position of each solve); in step\n    9c's words the robots' displacement (solver scale) > 1.0 m x s, the same test; both scales are recorded.\nWrites the evaluation json and (optionally) the pair npz in the step-7 format.\n\n    sonic_s1/bin/python -B system1/t14/objects/step9_eval.py --cand-dir <level dir with r0/ r1/> --source <source solve>         --gates <gates_m<tag>.json> --out <eval.json> [--pair-out <pair_fps30.npz>]\n",
 "shared_eval_rules": "T14 step 8: verdict and metrics of one candidate pair of the new partner construction (two robots solved around the shared\ntrajectory by role_solve.py). Read only, CPU.\n\nVerdict (existing numbers only, Kevin 2026-11-24 step-7 decision 4):\n  * V0 (scripts/reference_geometry_round2_checks.py, frozen) items named by Kevin:\n      gravity            relative_gravity_deviation_deg <= 5 (S's linear part vs the vertical; partner.gravity_deg);\n      support drift      <side>_support_added_drift_m <= 0.01 m per robot (V0 support windows of the source robot: foot bottom\n                         <= 4 cm, foot speed <= 0.15 m/s for >= 0.1 s; drift of the robot minus the source robot's; role 1's\n                         source = the source robot moved by S, whose drift is the same);\n      non-hand penetration  additional_nonhand_proxy_penetration_m <= 0.01 m per robot (round-2 CollisionProxy: robot vs the\n                         shared target minus the source robot vs the source object);\n      two-robot clearance   robot_robot_clearance_m >= -0.01 m (CollisionProxy, cross-robot OBB proxies);\n    (V0 support added speed is reported, not part of Kevin's list);\n  * section-4 contact acceptance: CoCarry contact retention >= 0.99 for each robot (person's hand within 0.10 m of the captured\n    object and the shared object moving faster than 0.03 m/s on the person's scale; robot hand signed distance >= -0.02 m,\n    exact convex distance to the target boxes). Section 4's penetration criterion compares with \"OmniRetarget as is\", which has\n    no result for these sequences; it is not used (reported numbers only);\n  * main motion of the shared trajectory (partner.main_motion, screen thresholds) \u2014 evaluated before solving.\nMetrics as rounds 6 / step 7: exact max penetration, robot-robot exact distance, 3-D contact-position error (person's palm ->\nnearest captured-surface point, moved by the role's region map; table family: capture -> training similarity first), hand\nmetrics, foot slide (posture_metrics rule), posture vs the person (posture_metrics.analyse on each robot's solve).\n\n    sonic_s1/bin/python -B system1/t14/objects/shared_eval.py --cand-dir <dir with r0/ r1/> --source <source solve> --out <json>\n",
 "command": "system1/t14/objects/step9_eval.py --cand-dir /home/kevin/duet-system1/logs_system1/t14/step9g/sub4_suitcase_042/m0p90 --source /home/kevin/duet-system1/logs_system1/t14/step9d/src/sub4_suitcase_042 --gates /home/kevin/duet-system1/logs_system1/t14/step9g/sub4_suitcase_042/gates_m0p90.json --out /home/kevin/duet-system1/logs_system1/t14/step9g/sub4_suitcase_042/m0p90/eval.json --pair-out /home/kevin/duet-system1/exports_system1/T14_references/step9g/sub4_suitcase_042_m0p90/pair_fps30.npz --r1-source construction"
}
